                  <p><strong>Indications &amp; Advantages &amp; Disadvantages:</strong> <mark class="hl-cause" data-pair="1">Enucleation is the treatment of choice for removal of cysts of the jaws that can be safely removed without unduly sacrificing adjacent structures.</mark> <mark class="hl-func" data-pair="2">Advantages: Pathologic examination of the entire cyst can be undertaken; initial excisional biopsy (i.e., enucleation) has also appropriately treated; no care for a marsupial cavity with constant irrigations needed.</mark> <mark class="hl-warn" data-pair="3">Disadvantages: Normal tissue may be jeopardized; fracture of the jaw; devitalization of teeth.</mark></p>
